{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupAction.Defs"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.exists_not_forall_eq_of_not_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.exists_not_forall_eq_of_not_central","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaloisOrbitTransport.lean#L104-L119","doc":"**Sharpness: commutativity in `eq_smul_of_transitive_orbit` cannot be dropped.**\n\nFor any group `G` acting on itself by left multiplication and any `b` that fails to\ncommute with something, right multiplication by `b` is equivariant, agrees with `b • ·`\nat the identity, and the identity generates -- yet it does not agree with `b • ·`\neverywhere.  So the conclusion genuinely needs `G` commutative, not merely the orbit\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.not_rel_of_transitive_orbit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.not_rel_of_transitive_orbit","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaloisOrbitTransport.lean#L89-L100","doc":"The contrapositive, spelled out: a negative verdict at one point of an orbit is a\nnegative verdict at every point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.rel_of_transitive_orbit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.rel_of_transitive_orbit","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaloisOrbitTransport.lean#L68-L87","doc":"**Agreement up to an action-stable relation propagates across an orbit, both ways.**\n\nStated as an `Iff`: the relation holds between two equivariant maps at every point of the\norbit precisely when it holds at the generating point.  So a *failure* at one point is a\nfailure at all of them, which is what makes a constant verdict down an orbit a theorem\nrather than a coincidence -- and a verdict that is NOT constant refutes a hypothesis\n(equivariance of one map, or stability of `r`) instead of distinguishing the points.\n\nNo commutativity is needed here; `r` being carried along by the action is enough. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.eq_smul_of_transitive_orbit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.eq_smul_of_transitive_orbit","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaloisOrbitTransport.lean#L53-L61","doc":"**One point suffices, on a single orbit.**  An equivariant map agreeing at `x₀` with\nthe action of `b` agrees with it everywhere on the orbit of `x₀`.\n\nCommutativity is used exactly once, to swap `g * b` for `b * g`; see\n`exists_not_forall_eq_of_not_central` for why it cannot be dropped. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.IsOrbitOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.IsOrbitOf","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaloisOrbitTransport.lean#L46-L48","doc":"`x₀` generates the whole space under the action -- the space is a single orbit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.IsEquivariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GaloisOrbitTransport.IsEquivariant","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaloisOrbitTransport.lean#L42-L44","doc":"`φ` commutes with the action: `φ (g • x) = g • φ x`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}